{"results": [{"id": "hp_doc_58cd71dec9c665e8f11eff4c6dd90af5944f3a54b69c3f0b0dd2ec36fe13d757", "title": "Temoer Terry", "text": "Temoer Terry (born June 12, 1975 in McPherson, Kansas) is a former college wrestling champion. Wrestling out of the University of Nebraska, (1994–1998), he had a collegiate record of 100-24. Terry had a record of 79-3 at McPherson High School. Terry has also coached at the college level for American University. Also coached for George Mason University", "score": 22.8567}, {"id": "hp_doc_e2e82376e9254615fce58ec92826995dd8fc5c3e8ed5c8ecb345680546623d14", "title": "Terry K. Amthor", "text": "Terry K. Amthor (born October 18, 1958) is an American game designer who has worked primarily on role-playing games, and as a fantasy author.", "score": 9.6228}, {"id": "hp_doc_1f131b42f62d5efbde937bbda5eed5b5e740f9d24bb707b0c375359713f28637", "title": "Marta Abreu", "text": "Marta Abreu de Estévez (13 November 1845 – 2 January 1909) was one of the most influential figures of her time in central Cuba, especially in her birth city and province of Santa Clara. For her constant aid to the poor, her donations to the city and the independence war, she won the title of “the great benefactor”.", "score": 9.5431}], "remaining_searches": 2}
