{"results": [{"id": "hp_doc_4c61662a67e4c7073ac87ddb0df58a3577119e01a3237bbae7312c68d1dbaeea", "title": "McPherson, Kansas", "text": "McPherson ( ) is a city in and the county seat of McPherson County, Kansas, United States, in the central part of the state. As of the 2010 census, the city population was 13,155. The city is named after Union General James Birdseye McPherson, a Civil War general. It is home to McPherson College and Central Christian College.", "score": 23.1115}, {"id": "hp_doc_58cd71dec9c665e8f11eff4c6dd90af5944f3a54b69c3f0b0dd2ec36fe13d757", "title": "Temoer Terry", "text": "Temoer Terry (born June 12, 1975 in McPherson, Kansas) is a former college wrestling champion. Wrestling out of the University of Nebraska, (1994–1998), he had a collegiate record of 100-24. Terry had a record of 79-3 at McPherson High School. Terry has also coached at the college level for American University. Also coached for George Mason University", "score": 17.6342}, {"id": "hp_doc_8b32f96de5d193a56f4dbeaaa57572231b824a7375f320f378eef02e4163e729", "title": "2006 Kansas Jayhawks football team", "text": "The 2006 Kansas Jayhawks football team represented the University of Kansas during the 2006 NCAA Division I FBS football season. They participated as members of the Big 12 Conference in the North Division. The team played their home games at Memorial Stadium in Lawrence, Kansas. They were coached by Mark Mangino.", "score": 9.7071}], "remaining_searches": 1}
